[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_4e76ea0753bad011\",\"r_3e85853b11b5bce5\"],null,null,[[\"rc_fd791be36a7542e0\",[\"Expert forecasts and secondary-market benchmarks project SpaceX's valuation to land between **$800 billion and $1.25 trillion** by the end of 2026, moving up from late-2025 insider tender offers that valued the company around $800 billion. \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Valuation Consensus \\u0026 Multiples Summary\\n\\n| Scenario | Implied Valuation Range | Implied Revenue Multiple (FY26E) | Primary Narrative / Baseline |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Bear Case** | **$550B – $700B** | ~24x – 30x | Regulatory delays on Starship, consumer Starlink churn/saturation, execution friction. |\\n| **Base Consensus** | **$800B – $1.0T** | ~35x – 43x | Continued Starlink enterprise scale ($18B+ run-rate) and launch cadence dominance. |\\n| **Bull / IPO Case** | **$1.25T – $1.5T** | ~50x – 65x | Rapid Direct-to-Cell rollout, Starship operational cadence, and pre-IPO positioning. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Upside Catalysts\\n\\n* **Starlink Unit Economics \\u0026 Direct-to-Cell Expansion:** Starlink accounts for the bulk of high-margin recurring cash flows. Commercialization of Direct-to-Cell mobile broadband (accelerated via spectrum deals such as EchoStar) substantially expands the Total Addressable Market (TAM) beyond fixed-broadband rural consumers into telecom backhaul and consumer\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,[[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\\u003dhttps://sacra.com/\\u0026client\\u003dBARD\\u0026type\\u003dFAVICON\\u0026size\\u003d256\\u0026fallback_opts\\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL\",\"https://sacra.com/c/spacex/valuation/\",\"SpaceX: $8