 run-rate) and launch cadence dominance.\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Bull / IPO Case\",[[0,15,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"$1.25T – $1.5T\",[[0,14,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"~50x – 65x\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Rapid Direct-to-Cell rollout, Starship operational cadence, and pre-IPO positioning.\"]]]]]]],true]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Key Upside Catalysts\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Starlink Unit Economics \\u0026 Direct-to-Cell Expansion: Starlink accounts for the bulk of high-margin recurring cash flows. Commercialization of Direct-to-Cell mobile broadband (accelerated via spectrum deals such as EchoStar) substantially expands the Total Addressable Market (TAM) beyond fixed-broadband rural consumers into telecom backhaul and consumer connectivity.\",[[0,51,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Starship Full Reusability \\u0026 Payload Cost Compression: Transitioning Starship from test flights to routine orbital payload delivery lowers launch costs per kilogram by over 80% compared to Falcon 9. This unlocks rapid deployment of larger Starlink V3 satellites and enables higher orbital launch frequency.\",[[0,53,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Defense\"]]]]]]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/expand/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1005,\"Shorter\",6,null,[\"compress\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/compress/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1002,\"Don't personalize\",2,null,[\"person_cancel\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/person_cancel/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1001,\"Try again\",1,null,[\"refresh\",\"https://fonts.