 (accelerated via spectrum deals such as EchoStar) substantially expands the Total Addressable Market (TAM) beyond fixed-broadband rural consumers into telecom backhaul and consumer connectivity.\",[[0,51,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Starship Full Reusability \\u0026 Payload Cost Compression: Transitioning Starship from test flights to routine orbital payload delivery lowers launch costs per kilogram by over 80% compared to Falcon 9. This unlocks rapid deployment of larger Starlink V3 satellites and enables higher orbital launch frequency.\",[[0,53,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Defense \\u0026 Sovereign Infrastructure Contracts: Broadened defense procurement through initiatives like Starshield, orbital tracking, and secure communications provides high-margin, multi-billion-dollar backlog stability alongside NASA Artemis milestones.\",[[0,45,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Potential Public Offering (IPO) Roadmap: While timing remains fluid, secondary market pricing continues to build in a liquidity/scarcity premium ahead of an eventual partial or full public listing.\",[[0,40,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Downside Risks\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Multiple Compression \\u0026 Tech Sentiment: Valuing SpaceX between 35x and 65x sales places it at a substantial premium compared to traditional aerospace/defense contractors (typically 1.5x–3x) and high-growth software/infrastructure firms (10x–20x). A broader macro contraction or rising cost of capital would pressure private secondary multiples.\",[[0,38,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Spectrum Allocation and Regulatory Hurdles: Direct-to-Cell services and Starlink orbital shell deployments face stringent regulatory scrutiny from the FCC, ITU, and local sovereign regulators, a